{"$message_type":"diagnostic","message":"mismatched types","code":{"code":"E0308","explanation":"Expected type did not match the received type.\n\nErroneous code examples:\n\n```compile_fail,E0308\nfn plus_one(x: i32) -> i32 {\n    x + 1\n}\n\nplus_one(\"Not a number\");\n//       ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ expected `i32`, found `&str`\n\nif \"Not a bool\" {\n// ^^^^^^^^^^^^ expected `bool`, found `&str`\n}\n\nlet x: f32 = \"Not a float\";\n//     ---   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^ expected `f32`, found `&str`\n//     |\n//     expected due to this\n```\n\nThis error occurs when an expression was used in a place where the compiler\nexpected an expression of a different type. It can occur in several cases, the\nmost common being when calling a function and passing an argument which has a\ndifferent type than the matching type in the function declaration.\n"},"level":"error","spans":[{"file_name":"examples\\gql_database_project.rs","byte_start":13076,"byte_end":13085,"line_start":397,"line_end":397,"column_start":13,"column_end":22,"is_primary":true,"text":[{"text":"            resolvers,","highlight_start":13,"highlight_end":22}],"label":"expected `dyn GQLResolver`, found `DefaultQueryResolver`","suggested_replacement":null,"suggestion_applicability":null,"expansion":null},{"file_name":"examples\\gql_database_project.rs","byte_start":12715,"byte_end":12767,"line_start":390,"line_end":390,"column_start":47,"column_end":99,"is_primary":false,"text":[{"text":"        resolvers.insert(\"Query\".to_string(), Arc::new(DefaultQueryResolver::new(storage.clone())));","highlight_start":47,"highlight_end":99}],"label":"this argument has type `Arc<DefaultQueryResolver>`...","suggested_replacement":null,"suggestion_applicability":null,"expansion":null},{"file_name":"examples\\gql_database_project.rs","byte_start":12677,"byte_end":12686,"line_start":390,"line_end":390,"column_start":9,"column_end":18,"is_primary":false,"text":[{"text":"        resolvers.insert(\"Query\".to_string(), Arc::new(DefaultQueryRes